00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.750
Within Word, as well as creating
documents from scratch, you can use a

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:07.440
wide range of pre formatted templates
to insert your information into.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:11.400
As you can see with the letter on
the screen in front of me, this

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.880
is a plain blank document that
I have then inserted all of the

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.560
information relating to a letter.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:21.150
However, if I wish to enhance the
document, make it look more professional,

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:26.759
I could format that and edit it add
images add charts, tables, shading, and

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:29.640
various other elements into the letter.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:32.850
Or alternatively, I could
access a preformatted template,

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:36.810
which will have all of that
information and formatting applied.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:43.980
So just to access the template files, I
would just click on the File menu, select

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:50.340
New and then I'm brought to the screen
with a wide range of templates available.

00:00:51.089 --> 00:00:54.570
So there are some templates on the
initial page, but you can access specific

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:59.400
templates such as business templates,
cards, flyers, letters educational types

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.440
of documents, resumes, and cover letters.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:07.770
So if I just select a letter and
then from the list, I can pick a

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.170
specific letter just to demonstrate.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.605
As you can see this has already been
provided with, formatting, there are

00:01:16.655 --> 00:01:20.595
spaces  for images, the text is broken
up into paragraphs and sections.

00:01:21.195 --> 00:01:25.455
There's a whole section relating to
the address, phone, email and website

00:01:25.455 --> 00:01:30.005
address and I could copy  that information
from that letter into that document.

00:01:30.905 --> 00:01:35.615
One of the things to bear in mind,
if you wish to insert specific images

00:01:35.705 --> 00:01:40.080
and change the content of your letter
to a certain style and in a certain

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:44.430
way, you will be better off using a
blank document because the template

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.170
already has the formatting applied.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:49.860
It is structured, has different
sections within it, and it can be

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.850
difficult to change those sections
without disrupting the layout

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:55.590
and presentation of the template.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:00.900
So, if you need to insert images,
charts, tables, and various other

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:04.890
elements within a letter, and you
need to have full control over that.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:08.430
You will be far better using an
existing document that you've created.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:13.430
And then you can save that as a
template rather than use a preformatted

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:16.500
template, which will have all of
the formatting already applied.

